# <Repo name>

<One paragraph: what this service/app is and who uses it.>

## Commands
- Install: `<npm ci | pip install -e .[dev] | ...>`
- Test: `<npm test | pytest | ...>`  (run this before every commit)
- Lint: `<npm run lint | ruff check . | ...>`
- Type check: `<tsc --noEmit | mypy | none>`
- Build: `<npm run build | none>`

## Linear
- team: <KEY>            # e.g. BE. Used by /next-ticket and /intake when no --team is given.
- project: <optional default project name>

## Branches and PRs
- Branch: `claude/<LINEAR-KEY>-<slug>` for agent work. Never commit to `main`.
- PR title: `<LINEAR-KEY>: <title>`. Body: acceptance-criteria checklist, how to verify, `Closes <issue url>`.
- Reviewers: <GitHub handles or "CODEOWNERS">
- Agents never merge, never force-push, never resolve review threads.

## Sensitive paths (reviewer treats changes here as high severity)
- <auth/, payments/, infra/, migrations/>

## Deploy
- Deploys happen in CD after merge. Production requires a human approval in the `production` environment.
- Agents do not run deploy commands. The denied commands are in `.claude/settings.json`.
- Release channel (Slack): `#<channel>`
- Changelog file: <CHANGELOG.md | none>
- Watch after deploy: <dashboard or log query>

## Conventions
- <Error handling, logging, naming, test layout. Keep to what a new engineer needs on day one.>
